Original commit body from bcc15616255b31d8745866df82c455e18829af8e:

tree-sitter parses erlang source, not preprocessed source, so
?LOG_DEBUG("...", [Secret]) produced no call edge at all -- no edge, no
catalogue match, no logging sink. rabbitmq writes 1,910 macro uses against
183 direct logger: calls, so the analyzer saw 9% of its logging surface.

SIZED BEFORE BUILT, as the item's own gate required. Expanding the macros
source-to-source across rabbitmq and running the six generic taint claims
cold on separate caches:

  host-secret-no-logging   68 -> 138 situations  (93 -> 2028 pairs)
  the other six claims     byte-identical

1,910 macro sites convert to +70 situations -- 3.7%. The item's hypothesis
that a recall hole no source reaches is worth less than its size suggests
is confirmed and quantified. Keyed on (source, caller) all 68 pre-expansion
situations survive; 61 re-root their sink from io:format to logger:*, which
is the coincidental coverage the io_lib removal predicted.

PREDICTION CONFIRMED BY AN INDEPENDENT MECHANISM. The transform arm forecast
138 rows; the shipped analyzer change on UNMODIFIED rabbitmq produces the
identical 138-row set and the same 1088 findings total.

THE GATE IS THE INCLUDE, NOT THE NAME. A ?LOG_ prefix match would sweep in
rabbitmq's ?LOG_DIR (a directory string), ?LOG_PREFIX (a prefix string) and
?LOG_EXCH_NAME (a binary). Requiring the file to include a header named
logger.hrl covers 2267 of 2267 sites across rabbitmq, emqx, ejabberd and
vernemq; the literal include_lib("kernel/include/logger.hrl") covers 2266.

THE PREPROCESSOR IS REFUSED ON MEASURED GROUNDS. General function-like macro
names are multiply-defined at 5-21% per repo, so a global name->body map is
ambiguous. The eight kernel names are never redefined in six repos. That
asymmetry is the whole argument, and it is recorded beside the vocabulary.

NOT COVERED, AND SAID SO: emqx's ?SLOG family (1,233 sites) and ejabberd's
?DEBUG/?INFO_MSG/... family (1,330). OTP's eight names are ~64% of the
corpus's macro-mediated logging.

New evidence type macro_expansion, priced 0.80/0.40 below ast_call, because
tree-sitter expanded nothing and evidence_type is how a consumer tells a
call the analyzer SAW from one it INFERRED.

